      "content": "thanks for understanding. it's hard to explain to anyone else because everyone just thinks i'm being forgetful. but the gaps in the journal feel so intentional. like the pages were just... neutralized. i looked up the biotech company that was based near my old city back then, \"Aethelgard Systems,\" and they did a lot of work with neural mapping and memory polymer research. it's too much of a coincidence. do you think there's a way to check if their server logs or old patent filings mention anything about \"reconstructive data management\" or similar tech for clinical use? i feel like if they were testing something, there might be a paper trail of the tech being developed even if my specific file was wiped.",
